  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Returned books need a brief condition check, and a return slip can record the book and its arrival.\", \"decision\": \"How should a returned book enter the checking queue?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nReaders hand over returned books, and helpers complete return slips during periodic grouped checks. The handover stays quick while recording and checking happen together later.\nHelpers accept returned books and complete the return slips during a brief intake conversation. Questions about a return are resolved before it enters the checking queue.\nReaders place returned books beside completed return slips, and helpers check them in arrival order. The slips preserve order without requiring a separate intake conversation."
    }
